<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Ngonde Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1891 CE (approx.) · capital Mbande</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small kingdom at the northern tip of Lake Malawi ruled by the Kyungu, a sacred king kept in ritual seclusion.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>According to tradition, the Kyungu dynasty arrived from the north-east and established itself over the farming and fishing people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karonga">Karonga</a> plain by around 1600. The capital at Mbande hill became the ritual centre of the kingdom.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Kyungu was a divine king whose health was linked to the land's fertility; he lived in seclusion, governed through a council of nobles (makambala) and, by tradition, was put to death if he fell seriously ill. Commoners grew bananas and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/millet">millet</a>, kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and fished in the lake, and the kingdom traded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and iron goods with neighbours.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 1880s the Swahili-Arab trader Mlozi set up fortified bases near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karonga">Karonga</a>, and the Ngonde were caught in the Karonga war of 1887–89 between Mlozi and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-lakes-company">African Lakes Company</a>. In 1891 the area became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-central-africa-protectorate">British Central Africa Protectorate</a>, later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nyasaland">Nyasaland</a>. The Kyungu remains a traditional ruler in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malawi">Malawi</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ngonde-kingdom.jpg" alt="Ngonde Kingdom" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown author Vector: Achim1999 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Malawi.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1891 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd